Split `src/types.ts` into `src/types/api.ts` and a new `src/types/content.ts`, re-exported from `src/types/index.ts` so every existing import keeps resolving. The new file describes `UserProfile` and `UserGroup` as Plone content, tied to `@plone/types` with `Pick` rather than `extends`: neither type carries Dublin Core or blocks behaviors, so most of `Content` is absent from the payload and inheriting it would promise fields no view can read. Every deviation is documented against a measured serialization. `providerFormSchema` and `clientFormSchema` are no longer `Record<string, any>`. @ericof
